WEBVTT

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:00.821
TL;DR

00:00:00.821 --> 00:00:02.061
Five layers: React/MUI, Flask

00:00:02.061 --> 00:00:02.501
APIs, analytics, edge execution,

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.581
and SQLite persistence.

00:00:03.581 --> 00:00:05.481
A bounded deque batches

00:00:05.481 --> 00:00:07.221
recent samples (500 records

00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:08.141
or ~5s) but is

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.021
not a durable queue.

00:00:09.021 --> 00:00:12.421
PHM uses RMS/FFT, One-Class SVM,

00:00:12.421 --> 00:00:13.701
DTW, and PCA drift

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:16.681
monitoring; engineers interpret results.

00:00:16.681 --> 00:00:18.801
AI agents are controlled clients:

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.081
the backend enforces allowlists, authorization,

00:00:21.081 --> 00:00:23.130
validation, and audit logging.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.641
Deployment starts as a Docker

00:00:24.641 --> 00:00:26.921
Compose edge monolith; decouple workers

00:00:26.921 --> 00:00:28.901
only when measurements justify it.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:31.601
Bottom line: Reliability comes from

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.181
traceable data, explicit failure

00:00:33.181 --> 00:00:34.530
behavior, and governed agents.
